# #1099 Stage 3: a table and a code block in HTML mode on the new editor. A new message is open,
# with focus in the To box. The table is typed as Markdown and carried into HTML mode.
w 4
q +{TAB}
w 2
q {TAB}
w 3

# 0. Into the body, in Markdown, and the content.
k %y
w 3
e Message body
q ^+2
w 3
Q Intro line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q | Name | Size |
q {ENTER}
Q |---|---|
q {ENTER}
Q | Apple | Twelve |
q {ENTER}
Q | Pear | Forty |
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Closing line
w 2
k ^+3
w 6
e Switched to HTML mode

# 1. Down through the table: one cell on each line, each read once and alone.
k ^{HOME}
w 3
e Intro line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Name
e! Size
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Size
e! Name
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Apple
e! Twelve
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Twelve
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Pear
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Forty
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Closing line

# 2. Where the caret is, asked in a cell.
k {UP}
w 3
e Forty
k ^t
w 5
e Table cell, row 3, column 2
k {UP}
w 2
k {UP}
w 2
k {UP}
w 3
e Apple
k ^t
w 5
e Table cell, row 2, column 1

# 3. Enter in a cell starts a second line in the same cell.
k {END}
w 2
k {ENTER}
w 3
t red ones
w 3
e red
k ^t
w 5
e Table cell, row 2, column 1
k {UP}
w 3
e Apple
k {DOWN}
w 3
e red ones
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Twelve
k ^t
w 5
e Table cell, row 2, column 2
